# tens and 200 (اثنين، اثني عشر، عشرين، مئتين): numbers in these lines nearly always follow a
# preposition or are objects ("في عشرين نقلة", "بفارق اثنين"), and these are the forms heard in
# spoken MSA. The plain words (3-10 with ة: ثلاثة) are also the forms for counting MASCULINE nouns.
# 21-99 compose units first: "{units} و{tens}" (ثلاثة وعشرين); 101-999: "{hundreds} و{rest}".
# Every hundred is listed. Numbers of 1000 and more have no words (the renderer says digits).
